{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-16649-r4637581","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Ukrainian Cabbage Soup (Kapusniak)","sourcePageId":16649,"sourceRevision":"4637581","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-05-26T02:27:22Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Ukrainian%20Cabbage%20Soup%20(Kapusniak)&oldid=4637581","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T16:29:16.734Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Boiled recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using cabbage","Category:Recipes using carrot","Category:Recipes using celery","Category:Recipes using chicken broth and stock","Category:Recipes using dill","Category:Recipes using garlic","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Soup recipes","Category:Ukrainian recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"dc88122589414ae30cf1aeb241748f99db4b6c647f63d2440f054e590202a830","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Soup recipes\n| Servings = 5\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of Ukraine|Ukrainian Cuisine]] | [[Cookbook:Soups|Soups]] \n\n'''Kapustnik''' is a hearty Central and Eastern European raw [[Cookbook:Cabbage|cabbage]] [[Cookbook:Soups|soup]]. It must be not confused with Kapusniak which is made of sauerkraut.\n\n==Ingredients==\n===Soup===\n*[[Cookbook:Olive Oil|Olive oil]]\n*2 medium-size [[Cookbook:Onion|onions]], peeled and [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n*2–5 cloves of [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]], peeled and [[Cookbook:Mincing|minced]]\n*1 litre or more [[Cookbook:Chicken Broth|chicken broth]]\n*1–2 [[Cookbook:Potato|potatoes]], peeled and cut into bite-sized pieces\n*4–6 [[Cookbook:Carrot|carrots]], peeled and cut into bite-sized pieces\n*4–5 sticks of [[Cookbook:Celery|celery]], sliced into bite-sized pieces\n*Pickling spices\n*[[Cookbook:Sage|Sage]]\n*[[Cookbook:Thyme|Thyme]]\n*[[Cookbook:Oregano|Oregano]]\n*[[Cookbook:Bay Leaf|Bay leaves]], \n*[[Cookbook:Rosemary|Rosemary]]\n*[[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]]\n*[[Cookbook:Pepper|Pepper]]\n*[[Cookbook:Worcestershire Sauce|Worcestershire sauce]]\n*[[Cookbook:Soy Sauce|Soy sauce]]\n*[[Cookbook:Seasoning Salt|Seasoning salt]]\n*[[Cookbook:Garlic Salt|Garlic salt]]\n*[[Cookbook:Celery Salt|Celery salt]]\n*1 large can of diced [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomatoes]]\n*1 head of [[Cookbook:Cabbage|cabbage]], sliced\n*Fresh [[Cookbook:Dill|dill]], chopped\n\n===Garnish===\n*[[Cookbook:Sour Cream|Sour cream]] or [[Cookbook:Yoghurt|yoghurt]]\n\n==Procedure==\n# In a large cooking pot heat about 3–4 tablespoons of olive oil. Add the onions and garlic, along with more olive oil if necessary. Let the onions and garlic cook over medium or low heat for 8–10 minutes.\n# Add the chicken broth, and bring to a [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]].\n# Add the potatoes, carrots, celery, and spices; bring to a boil, and [[Cookbook:Simmering|simmer]] over medium heat until vegetables are almost tender enough to eat. If the soup becomes too thick, add some more chicken broth, but it should be a hearty soup with plenty of vegetables.\n# Season with salt, pepper, Worcestershire sauce, soy sauce, seasoning salt, garlic salt, and or celery salt as desired.\n# Add the can of tomatoes and the shredded cabbage. Again, let the soup simmer over medium heat; continue tasting to see whether your imagination has worked magic.\n# Lastly, add the chopped fresh dill.\n# When it’s done, serve [[Cookbook:Garnish|garnished]] with sour cream.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using cabbage]]\n[[Category:Soup recipes]]\n[[Category:Boiled recipes]]\n[[Category:Ukrainian recipes]]\n\n[[Category:Recipes using carrot]]\n[[Category:Recipes using celery]]\n[[Category:Recipes using dill]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chicken broth and stock]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Ukrainian Cabbage Soup (Kapusniak)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"5","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"Olive oil","sourceText":"Olive oil","amountText":"Olive oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"2 medium-size onions, peeled and chopped","sourceText":"2 medium-size onions, peeled and chopped","amountText":"2 medium-size onions, peeled and chopped","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"2–5 cloves of garlic, peeled and minced","sourceText":"2–5 cloves of garlic, peeled and minced","amountText":"2–5 cloves of garlic, peeled and minced","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 litre or more chicken broth","sourceText":"1 litre or more chicken broth","amountText":"1 litre or more chicken broth","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"1–2 potatoes, peeled and cut into bite-sized pieces","sourceText":"1–2 potatoes, peeled and cut into bite-sized pieces","amountText":"1–2 potatoes, peeled and cut into bite-sized pieces","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"4–6 carrots, peeled and cut into bite-sized pieces","sourceText":"4–6 carrots, peeled and cut into bite-sized pieces","amountText":"4–6 carrots, peeled and cut into bite-sized pieces","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","n